## The Challenge

### The Japanese dining market in India is crowded, but often feels inauthentic.

Many restaurants just copy the "look" of Japan without understanding the culture, making them feel like temporary themes rather than serious brands. Our challenge was to create a brand that felt high-end, respectful, and real. We had to avoid the usual clichés. In the premium sector, customers spot "fake" concepts immediately, so we needed a design that built trust before the customer even tasted the food.

