### The word "Akebono" (曙) literally means "Dawn" or "Daybreak" in Japanese.

### "Fuji" (The Peak): Represents the highest standard of quality and authenticity.

## The Solution

### We focused on a simple idea: "The Journey."

- **The Logo:** We combined the Torii Gate (which creates an entrance) with Mount Fuji (representing the peak of quality) and a Red Sun (symbolizing the dawn). It is a calm, powerful symbol that invites people in rather than shouting at them.
- **The Look:** We chose a "Dawn Red" and soft neutral colors to feel expensive but welcoming.
- **The System:** We didn't just make a logo; we designed the whole business. We applied this clean look to menus, chopstick sleeves, takeout packaging, and billboards. Every item looks like it belongs to the same family.

![Akebono Fuji case study image](../../assets/projects/akebono-fuji/Color-Moodboard-Akibono.webp)

